    "why_parked": "The takes recorded for this kind have been read once and the unit is not being asked again for it. What is kept: a wah's manual byte climbs, monotonically, over the whole of the range asked, on the one type read. What is given up is a law in the byte, because no row of this kind was read standing still and clear of anything in front of the band set: the one wah admitted was swept by its own modulator, the other wah was read through an overdrive, both phasers were swept by theirs, and the noise low-pass acts on a hum that stands under the stimulus, where it lifts a few bottom bands and no corner can be read off the band set.",
