  "claim": "A wah's manual byte moves its band-pass up the spectrum at every setting asked from 32: on 04 04 the band the profile peaks in climbs from 746 Hz at 32 to 4486 Hz at 127, 2.59 octaves, and not along a straight line in octaves -- at 55 it sits 0.34 octaves under one, against takes that agree to 0.084. That was read with the type's own modulator sweeping the filter through every take, so what climbs is where a moving filter spends its time rather than where the byte puts it, and of the other rows read for this kind, the noise low-pass moves a hum that stands under the stimulus by at most 3.1 dB in one band, two phasers were read with their own modulator running and the second wah through an overdrive. No law in the byte is set for a corner or a centre, and none is carried to another type.",
